# ZX81 ULA 2C210, gate-level netlist transcribed from Ferranti drawing LD6679/ULA2C210/1 issue 1 (12/01/82).
# Started from the 2C184 transcription (ula/2c184.net): the two drawings share the grid and most of the logic.
# Every line still has to be checked against the 2C210 drawing; lines checked carry 'ok210'.
# Format: see README.md. Grid squares are row then column, as printed on the drawing's edges: the column whose edge
# tick is nearest the symbol's centre, and the row nearest it (all re-read from the scan when ula/draw_2c210.js was
# written, so the redrawn sheet lines up with the original).

# ---- power ----
# Gate power, pwr=: R (single current source), R/2 (double) or R/3 (treble), as marked on the drawing. Every mark was
# found by template matching the whole scan (37 marks: 33 gates, and the four on the Q19 cell) and read by eye; a gate
# with no mark is R. The simulator takes each gate's delay from Ferranti's Table 2.1 (ULA2C000/5C000 gate delays,
# typical at 25 C) by its power, its fan-in and its fan-out (the inputs its output drives). See ula/README.md.
VCC     pin_in   VCC            PN40   @1A  ok210
GND     pin_in   GND            PN34   @37A  ok210

# ---- data pins D0-D7: 16K pull-up, then an emitter-follower input buffer ----
# The pin node itself (nDn) is also driven by the keyboard and port outputs (open collector, rows 12-19).
pD0     pin_io   nD0            PN32   @3B   pullup=16k  ok210
pD1     pin_io   nD1            PN30   @4B   pullup=16k  ok210
pD2     pin_io   nD2            PN28   @5B   pullup=16k  ok210
pD3     pin_io   nD3            PN26   @6B   pullup=16k  ok210
pD4     pin_io   nD4            PN24   @7B   pullup=16k  ok210
pD5     pin_io   nD5            PN23   @8B   pullup=16k  ok210
pD6     pin_io   nD6            PN21   @9B   pullup=16k  ok210
pD7     pin_io   nD7            PN19   @10B  pullup=16k  ok210
bD0     buf_ef   D0             nD0    @3N  ok210
bD1     buf_ef   D1             nD1    @4N  ok210
bD2     buf_ef   D2             nD2    @5N  ok210
bD3     buf_ef   D3             nD3    @6N  ok210
bD4     buf_ef   D4             nD4    @7N  ok210
bD5     buf_ef   D5             nD5    @8N  ok210
bD6     buf_ef   D6             nD6    @9N  ok210
bD7     buf_ef   D7             nD7    @10N  ok210

# ---- other input pins (16K pull-up, emitter-follower buffer) ----
pKB0    pin_in   nKB0           PN33   @12B  pullup=16k  ok210
pKB1    pin_in   nKB1           PN31   @13B  pullup=16k  ok210
pKB2    pin_in   nKB2           PN29   @14B  pullup=16k  ok210
pKB3    pin_in   nKB3           PN27   @15B  pullup=16k  ok210
pKB4    pin_in   nKB4           PN25   @16B  pullup=16k  ok210
pUSA    pin_in   nUSA           PN22   @17B  pullup=16k  ok210
pTAPE   pin_in   nTAPE          PN20   @18B  series=400R clamp=diode-to-GND divider=5k-to-VS  ok210
pOSC    osc      OSC            PN35   @21B  ceramic resonator  ok210
pMREQ   pin_in   nMREQ          PN9    @23B  pullup=16k  ok210
pM1     pin_in   nM1            PN10   @24B  pullup=16k  ok210
pA15    pin_in   nA15           PN18   @26B  pullup=16k  ok210
pHALT   pin_in   nHALT          PN17   @27B  pullup=16k  ok210
pA14    pin_in   nA14           PN11   @29B  pullup=16k  ok210
pWR     pin_in   nWR            PN8    @32B  pullup=16k  ok210
pIORQ   pin_in   nIORQ          PN7    @34B  pullup=16k  ok210
pRD     pin_in   nRD            PN6    @36B  pullup=16k  ok210
bKB0    buf_ef   KB0            nKB0   @12D  note=(3VBE)  ok210
bKB1    buf_ef   KB1            nKB1   @13D  note=(3VBE)  ok210
bKB2    buf_ef   KB2            nKB2   @14D  note=(3VBE)  ok210
bKB3    buf_ef   KB3            nKB3   @15D  note=(3VBE)  ok210
bKB4    buf_ef   KB4            nKB4   @16D  note=(3VBE)  ok210
bUSA    buf_ef   USA            nUSA   @17E  ok210
iTAPE   inv      TAPE           nTAPE  @18E pwr=R  inverter drawn with output circle  ok210
bMREQ   buf_ef   N.MREQ         nMREQ  @23D  ok210
bM1     buf_ef   N.M1           nM1    @24D  ok210
bA15    buf_ef   A15            nA15   @26D  ok210
bHALT   buf_ef   N.HALT         nHALT  @27D  ok210
bA14    buf_ef   A14            nA14   @29D  ok210
bWR     buf_ef   N.WR           nWR    @32D  ok210
bIORQ   buf_ef   N.IORQ         nIORQ  @34D  ok210
bRD     buf_ef   N.RD           nRD    @36D  ok210

# ---- output pins ----
# PN14 N.Ø (clock to the Z80, row 2), PN15 N.NMI (row 5, open collector with 5K to VCC), PN16 TV/TAPE (row 10,
# 3-level output from N.SYNC and N.VIDEO), PN36-39 and PN1-2 A3'-A8' (rows 12-17), PN5/4/3 A0'-A2' (rows 21-23),
# PN12 RAM N.CS and PN13 ROM N.CS (rows 30-32, RTL stages "see cct diagram").

# ---- port read and the NOP: open-collector drivers onto the data pins (rows 12-19, columns G-K) ----
# EN = "not reading the port" (high: the drivers let go), from the R/2 inverter at 20K. FORCE = pull the data low
# (the NOP fed to the Z80 for a character), vertical at column W. Checked: row 12 drives D0 ... row 19 drives D7.
kb0a    nor2     n_12R          KB0 EN        @12G pwr=R  ok210
kb0b    nor2     n_12V          n_12R FORCE   @12I pwr=R/2  ok210
kb0c    pin_oc   nD0            n_12V         @12K   drives D0 low when n_12V is low  ok210
kb1a    nor2     n_13R          KB1 EN        @13G pwr=R  ok210
kb1b    nor2     n_13V          n_13R FORCE   @13I pwr=R/2  ok210
kb1c    pin_oc   nD1            n_13V         @13K  ok210
kb2a    nor2     n_14R          KB2 EN        @14G pwr=R  ok210
kb2b    nor2     n_14V          n_14R FORCE   @14I pwr=R/2  ok210
kb2c    pin_oc   nD2            n_14V         @14K  ok210
kb3a    nor2     n_15R          KB3 EN        @15G pwr=R  ok210
kb3b    nor2     n_15V          n_15R FORCE   @15I pwr=R/2  ok210
kb3c    pin_oc   nD3            n_15V         @15K  ok210
kb4a    nor2     n_16R          KB4 EN        @16G pwr=R  ok210
kb4b    nor2     n_16V          n_16R FORCE   @16I pwr=R/2  ok210
kb4c    pin_oc   nD4            n_16V         @16K  ok210
d5a     inv      n_17V          FORCE         @17I pwr=R/2   D5 has no input: it reads high (pull-up), and is pulled low for the NOP  ok210
d5c     pin_oc   nD5            n_17V         @17K  ok210
usaa    nor2     n_17R          USA EN        @17G pwr=R  ok210
usab    inv      n_18V          n_17R         @18I pwr=R/2   D6 is not forced for the NOP (a character byte has D6 low already)  ok210
usac    pin_oc   nD6            n_18V         @18K  ok210
tapa    nor2     n_18R          TAPE EN       @18G pwr=R  ok210
tapb    nor2     n_19V          n_18R FORCE   @19I pwr=R/2  ok210
tapc    pin_oc   nD7            n_19V         @19K  ok210
en      inv      EN             INFE          @20F pwr=R/2   ok210; R/2; INFE comes up column L from the fsr gate's input (row 37.8) to row 20.4

# ---- dot shift register Q1-Q8 (rows 3-10, columns T-AL) ----
# Inverters A-H take D0-D7. Each stage's reset is NOR(~Dn, S/L, D6L): with S/L and D6L low, a 1 in the ROM byte
# clears that stage. Stages shift on the falling edge of SCLK (the clock pins carry a bubble), Q1 shifting in a 1.
iA      inv      nA             D0            @6T pwr=R  ok210
iB      inv      nB             D1            @6V pwr=R  ok210
iC      inv      nC             D2            @6X pwr=R  ok210
iD      inv      nD             D3            @6Z pwr=R  ok210
iE      inv      nE             D4            @6AB pwr=R  ok210
iF      inv      nF             D5            @6AD pwr=R  ok210
iG      inv      nG             D6            @6AF pwr=R  ok210
iH      inv      nH             D7            @6AH pwr=R  ok210
rA      nor3     R1             nA S/L D6L    @8T pwr=R/2  ok210
rB      nor3     R2             nB S/L D6L    @8V pwr=R/2  ok210
rC      nor3     R3             nC S/L D6L    @8X pwr=R/2  ok210
rD      nor3     R4             nD S/L D6L    @8Z pwr=R/2  ok210
rE      nor3     R5             nE S/L D6L    @8AB pwr=R/2  ok210
rF      nor3     R6             nF S/L D6L    @8AD pwr=R/2  ok210
rG      nor3     R7             nG S/L D6L    @8AF pwr=R/2  ok210
rH      nor3     R8             nH S/L D6L    @8AH pwr=R/2  ok210
Q1      dff      Q1             VCC ~SCLK R1  @10T pwr=R  D tied to '1'  ok210
Q2      dff      Q2             Q1  ~SCLK R2  @10V pwr=R  ok210
Q3      dff      Q3             Q2  ~SCLK R3  @10X pwr=R  ok210
Q4      dff      Q4             Q3  ~SCLK R4  @10Z pwr=R  ok210
Q5      dff      Q5             Q4  ~SCLK R5  @10AB pwr=R  ok210
Q6      dff      Q6             Q5  ~SCLK R6  @10AD pwr=R  ok210
Q7      dff      Q7             Q6  ~SCLK R7  @10AF pwr=R  ok210
Q8      dff      Q8             Q7  ~SCLK R8  @10AH pwr=R  ok210

# ---- character latch NQ11-NQ18 (row 14, columns T-AH): D-type latches, inverted outputs ----
# Inputs checked: NQ11 D0, NQ12 D1, NQ13 D2, NQ14 D3, NQ15 D4, NQ16 D5. Latch clock LCLK is driven by two R/3
# inverters in parallel (rows 18-19, columns AE and AG) from LCLKn.
lck1    inv      LCLK           LCLKn         @17X  pwr=R/3  R/3  ok210
lck2    inv      LCLK           LCLKn         @17Z  pwr=R/3  R/3 (in parallel with lck1)  ok210
NQ11    dlatch   NQ11           D0 ~LCLK      @14T pwr=R   output inverted  ok210
NQ12    dlatch   NQ12           D1 ~LCLK      @14V pwr=R  ok210
NQ13    dlatch   NQ13           D2 ~LCLK      @14X  pwr=R  ok210
NQ14    dlatch   NQ14           D3 ~LCLK      @14Z  pwr=R  ok210
NQ15    dlatch   NQ15           D4 ~LCLK      @14AB pwr=R?  ok210
NQ16    dlatch   NQ16           D5 ~LCLK      @14AD pwr=R?  ok210
Q17     dlatch   Q17            CHAR ~LCLK    @14AF pwr=R  ok210; true output; D: the row 13.8 line, down column R to the CHAR line at row 19.4 (so Q17 holds 'this fetch was a character', not D6 itself)
d6l     inv      D6L            Q17           @12AH pwr=R/3  ok210; R/3; low after a character fetch; its output also runs up column AN to the shift register's D6L line
NQ18    dlatch   NQ18           D7 ~LCLK      @14AH pwr=R  ok210; D from the row 11.4 line (D7)
# video (rows 12-15, columns AL-AT), 2C210 as drawn: Q32 holds the inverse-video bit; four NORs make VID = XNOR(Q8, Q32)
q32d    nor2     n_q32d         D6L NQ18      @13AL pwr=R  ok210
Q32     dff      Q32            n_q32d ~S/L -     @13AN pwr=R  ok210; clocked by S/L (column AJ): it takes the inverse bit when the byte is loaded; no reset drawn
vx      nor2     VX             Q8 Q32        @13AP pwr=R  ok210; SV = Q8 (Q8's output runs right to column AM and down)
vy      nor2     VY             Q8 VX         @12AR pwr=R  ok210
vz      nor2     VZ             VX Q32        @14AR pwr=R  ok210
vid     nor2     VID            VY VZ         @13AT pwr=R/2  ok210; R/2. VID = XNOR(Q8, Q32)

# ---- line counter Q21-Q28 (row 5, columns AL-AZ): ripple toggle stages, each clocked on the falling edge of
# the previous stage's true output; all reset together by CRES (row 6.5). Inverted outputs marked n.
Q21     tff      Q21 Q21n       ~CCLK CRES    @5AL pwr=R   ok210; CCLK: the clock (column AK) delayed by four inverters
Q22     tff      Q22 Q22n       ~Q21 CRES     @5AN pwr=R  ok210
Q23     tff      Q23 Q23n       ~Q22 CRES     @5AP pwr=R  ok210
Q24     tff      Q24 Q24n       ~Q23 CRES     @5AR pwr=R  ok210
Q25     tff      Q25 Q25n       ~Q24 CRES     @5AT pwr=R  ok210
Q26     tff      Q26 Q26n       ~Q25 CRES     @5AV pwr=R  ok210
Q27     tff      Q27 Q27n       ~Q26 CRES     @5AX pwr=R  ok210
Q28     tff      Q28 Q28n       ~Q27 CRES     @5AZ pwr=R  ok210
# count 207 = Q28 Q27 Q24 Q23 Q22 Q21 high, Q26 Q25 low: the 8-input NOR goes high and resets the counter,
# so a line is 207 counts (checked against the known 207 T-state line).
c207    nor8     T207           Q28n Q27n Q26 Q25 Q21n Q22n Q23n Q24n   @8AX pwr=R  ok210
# CRES: see crn (row 11): count 207 or INTACK
LS      nor4     LINE-SYNC      Q25n Q26 Q27 Q28   @3BA pwr=R   high for counts 16-31: 16 counts of horizontal sync  ok210

# ---- NMI, sync and clock outputs (rows 2-11, columns BB-BJ) ----
nm1     inv      n_5BG          LINE-SYNC     @5BB pwr=R  ok210
nm2     nor2     n_5BI          n_5BG NMIOFF  @5BD pwr=R   NMIOFF from the NMI latch (nl2)  ok210
nm3     inv      n_5BL          n_5BI         @5BF pwr=R  ok210
nm4     pin_oc   N.NMI          n_5BL         @5BH   PN15, 5K pull-up to VCC on chip  ok210
fs1     nor2     SYNCn          LINE-SYNC FRAME-SYNC   @8BB pwr=R  ok210
fs2     inv      N.SYNC         SYNCn         @8BD pwr=R/2   R/2  ok210
tv      out3     TV/TAPE        N.SYNC N.VIDEO   @10BG   PN16, '3 level output'; circuit on ULA 2C158/2: N.SYNC high pulls the output to 0 V; otherwise N.VIDEO high gives the lower level (black, about 2.8 V), low the higher (white, about 4.3 V); 200 ohms in series  ok210
ck1     inv      n_2BH          CLKSRC        @2BD pwr=R/2   R/2; CLKSRC = Q19, up column AK  ok210
ck2     pin_tp   N.PHI          n_2BH         @2BF   PN14, totem-pole output  ok210; the cell does not invert (circuit 'PIN phi-bar' on ULA 2C158/2: input transistor, phase splitter, totem pole), so N.PHI = NOT Q19 and the Z80's CLK (through TR2, an inverter) = Q19: the latch windows fall after CLK falls in T1 and T2, and FORCE covers the T3 rise when the Z80 takes the NOP

# ---- clock: oscillator, Q19, the counter clock (rows 17-25, columns N-AL) ----
oscb    inv      OSCn           OSC           @21F pwr=R   inverter after the oscillator cell and a cross-under  ok210
Q19     tff      Q19 Q19n       ~OSCn -       @21O pwr=R/2   ok210; R/2 cell; clocked from the oscillator line; no reset drawn; Q19 = 3.25 MHz
# CLKSRC (the line that goes up column AK to row 2 and right to the N.PHI output) is Q19's true output (row 21). ok210
alias   CLKSRC   Q19
cc1     inv      n_cc1          Q19           @9AK pwr=R   four inverters in series delay Q19 into the counter clock  ok210
cc2     inv      n_cc2          n_cc1         @9AM pwr=R  ok210
cc3     inv      n_cc3          n_cc2         @8AM pwr=R  ok210
cc4     inv      CCLK           n_cc3         @8AK pwr=R  ok210
cr      inv      CRES           CRESn         @11AS pwr=R/3  R/3  ok210
crn     nor2     CRESn          T207 INTACK   @11AU pwr=R  ok210; drawn pointing left; INTACK comes up column AV from row 27.3: the line counter restarts at count 207 and at every interrupt acknowledge

# ---- delay chains (rows 17-24) ----
# Chain A (row 17): R/? inverter output up at 17N, then three NOR2 gates with both inputs tied (inverters).
# Chain B (row 21-22): from Q19n, NOR2 gates with both inputs tied, five or more in series.
# Chain C (row 24): NOR2 gates with both inputs tied, from the row 24 vertical at column R.
# LCLKn = NOR4(chain A out, col W vertical from row 13, the row 18 line from column O, Q19)   @18X   R/3
dA0     inv      DA0            OSCn          @18N pwr=R   ok210; input from the column N vertical down to the oscillator line (row 21)
sck     inv      SCLK           DA0           @16N pwr=R/3   ok210; R/3; output up column N to row 13.5, right, up column W to the shift register clocks (row 11.3): the dots shift at 6.5 MHz
dA1     nor2     DA1            DA0 DA0       @17O pwr=R  ok210
dA2     nor2     DA2            DA1 DA1       @17Q pwr=R  ok210
dA3     nor2     DA3            DA2 DA2       @17S pwr=R  ok210
lckn    nor4     LCLKn          DA1 DA3 N.M1 Q19   @18V pwr=R/3   ok210; R/3; DA1 via row 16.3; N.M1 via column O and row 18.3
i19     inv      n_i19          CHAR          @19S pwr=R   ok210; CHAR comes up column O to row 19.4
lk2     nor3     FORCE          LCLKn N.M1 n_i19   @18AB pwr=R/3  ok210; R/3, 2C210 only; LK2 on the drawing: high when LCLKn is low in an M1 character fetch; down to row 19.8, left, and up column I as FORCE
dB1     nor2     DB1            Q19n Q19n     @22Q pwr=R  ok210
dB2     nor2     DB2            DB1 DB1       @22S pwr=R  ok210
dB3     nor2     DB3            DB2 DB2       @22V  pwr=R  ok210
dB4     nor2     DB4            DB3 DB3       @22X  pwr=R  ok210
dB5     nor2     DB5            DB4 DB4       @22Z  pwr=R  ok210
dC1     nor2     DC1            N.MREQ N.MREQ @25V pwr=R  ok210
dC2     nor2     DC2            DC1 DC1       @25X  pwr=R  ok210
dC3     nor2     DC3            DC2 DC2       @25Z  pwr=R  ok210
d21     nor3     n_22AJ         Q19n DB5 DC3  @22AB pwr=R/2  ok210; R/2; Q19n along row 21.7 from Q19 and down column AB
d21b    inv      S/L            n_22AJ        @22AE pwr=R/3  ok210; R/3; this is S/L: right along row 22.3, up column AJ to the shift register (and Q32's clock)
aen1    nor2     AENa           D6L M1        @25AI pwr=R  ok210; D6L from d6l's output via row 13.6, column AJ, row 16.2 and down column AG (it crosses the S/L line at row 22.3 without a dot); M1 via row 28.6 and column AD; AENa also runs left along row 25.9 to Q20's D input. So the ULA drives A0'-A8' from the end of a character's M1 to the next M1
aen2    inv      n_aen2         AENa          @25AL pwr=R  ok210
aen3    inv      AENin          n_aen2        @25AN pwr=R/2  ok210; R/2; up column AU to the address enable (row 18)

# ---- address outputs (rows 12-27, columns BC-BJ) ----
# A3'-A8': the latch's inverted outputs are inverted again and driven through tri-state buffers. The buffers' enables
# (active low) share AEN, made by an RTL inverter with a 1.8K pull-up (row 18) from AENin (the long row 18 line).
aen     inv_rtl  AEN            AENin         @18BE  ok210; RTL, 1.8K pull-up
oa3     inv      n_oa3          NQ11          @12BC pwr=R  ok210
oa4     inv      n_oa4          NQ12          @13BC pwr=R  ok210
oa5     inv      n_oa5          NQ13          @14BC pwr=R  ok210
oa6     inv      n_oa6          NQ14          @15BC pwr=R  ok210
oa7     inv      n_oa7          NQ15          @16BC pwr=R  ok210
oa8     inv      n_oa8          NQ16          @17BC pwr=R  ok210
pa3     pin_ts   A3'            n_oa3 ~AEN    @12BG  PN36  ok210
pa4     pin_ts   A4'            n_oa4 ~AEN    @13BG  PN37  ok210
pa5     pin_ts   A5'            n_oa5 ~AEN    @14BG  PN38  ok210
pa6     pin_ts   A6'            n_oa6 ~AEN    @15BG  PN39  ok210
pa7     pin_ts   A7'            n_oa7 ~AEN    @16BG  PN1  ok210
pa8     pin_ts   A8'            n_oa8 ~AEN    @17BG  PN2  ok210
# row counter Q29, Q30, NQ31 (rows 19-23, columns BB-BD): ripple toggles, reset together by RRES (column BA)
Q29     tff      Q29 Q29n       ~SYNCn FRAME-SYNC  @19BB pwr=R  ok210; reset: FRAME-SYNC, via column BA; clock: SYNCn (fs1's output), down column BB, so the row counter steps as each sync pulse starts
Q30     tff      Q30 Q30n       ~Q29 FRAME-SYNC     @21BB pwr=R  ok210
NQ31    tff      - NQ31         ~Q30 FRAME-SYNC     @23BB pwr=R  only the inverted output is drawn  ok210
oa0     inv      n_oa0          Q29n          @20BE pwr=R  ok210
oa1     inv      n_oa1          Q30n          @21BE pwr=R  ok210
oa2     inv      n_oa2          NQ31          @22BE pwr=R  ok210
pa0     pin_ts   A0'            n_oa0 ~AEN    @20BG  PN5, also read back (below)  ok210
pa1     pin_ts   A1'            n_oa1 ~AEN    @21BG  PN4, also read back  ok210
pa2     pin_ts   A2'            n_oa2 ~AEN    @22BG  PN3  ok210
# A0' and A1' are read back into the chip for the port decode
ba0     buf_ef   A0in           A0'           @26BG  ok210
ba1     buf_ef   A1in           A1'           @27BG  ok210

# ---- character fetch decode (row 26, columns F-I), 2C210 as drawn ----
a15i    inv      A15n           A15           @26F pwr=R   ok210
hlti    inv      HALTn          N.HALT        @27F pwr=R   ok210
chr     nor4     CHAR           D6 N.MREQ A15n HALTn   @26I pwr=R/2   ok210; R/2; high for a memory read from A15 high with D6 low while not halted; top input is D6, via column M and the row 13.0 line
# ---- memory request logic (rows 23-30, columns Q-X), traced on the 2C210 ----
# N.MREQ runs down column R/S: into chain C (row 24), the two select NORs and Q20's clock. N.M1 turns down column R to
# the inverter at row 26.5, whose output M1 resets Q20 and runs right along row 28.6, up column AD to row 24.4 (aen1).
m1i     inv      M1             N.M1          @26U pwr=R   ok210
a14i    inv      A14n           A14           @29Q pwr=R   ok210
romacc  nor2     ROMACC         N.MREQ A14    @27T pwr=R   ok210; high for a memory cycle with A14 low
ramacc  nor2     RAMACC         N.MREQ A14n   @29T pwr=R   ok210; high for a memory cycle with A14 high; runs right along row 29 to the RAM select
Q20     dff      Q20            AENa ~N.MREQ M1   @27X pwr=R   ok210; clocked as MREQ goes low; reset by M1; D is AENa (row 25.9, from aen1): set when the ULA drives the address
romln   nor2     ROMLINE        Q20 ROMACC    @30W pwr=R   ok210; runs right along row 30 to the ROM select
rmin    inv      RAMSELn        RAMACC        @30AS pwr=R  ok210

# ---- I/O decode and vertical sync (rows 30-37, columns E-Z) ----
# N.WR turns up at column H to row 30.6, N.IORQ at column I to row 31.0, N.RD at column J to row 31.4.
iowr    nor2     IOWR           N.WR N.IORQ   @33K pwr=R   ok210; high for any I/O write: clears vertical sync
intack  nor2     INTACK         N.IORQ N.M1   @35K pwr=R   ok210; high during the interrupt acknowledge (IORQ and M1 both low); runs right to row 35.4, column AK, and up
fsl     nor3     FRAME-SYNC     NMION IOWR FSL   @33O pwr=R/2   ok210; R/2; held off while the NMI is on, cleared by any OUT
fsr     nor2     FSL            FRAME-SYNC INFE  @37O pwr=R   ok210; cross-coupled with fsl: IN with A0 low starts vertical sync

# ---- 2C210 only: blanking (row 1, columns AT-BA) ----
bl1     inv      n_bl1          Q25           @1AT pwr=R   ok210
bl2     inv      n_bl2          n_bl1         @1AV pwr=R   ok210
bl3     inv      Q25nd          n_bl2         @1AX pwr=R   ok210; Q25 inverted and delayed by three gates
blank   nor4     BLANK          Q25nd Q26 Q27 Q28   @1BA pwr=R   ok210; LINE-SYNC with its start delayed by the three inverters
vb      nor2     n_vb           BLANK VID     @11BB pwr=R  ok210; VID from vid (row 13.2, right and up)
vbi     inv      N.VIDEO        n_vb          @11BD pwr=R/2  ok210; R/2. The 2C210 blanks the picture during line sync
# ---- differences from the 2C184 seen so far (to be transcribed in full) ----
# 1. Rows 1-2, columns AT-BA: a new chain of three inverters fed from Q25 (vertical at column AU) into a NOR at
#    row 1, column BA; it feeds the LINE-SYNC / NMI area. The 2C184 has nothing here.
# 2. Rows 9-10, columns AZ-BB: N.VIDEO now comes from a NOR2 (one input from the row 13 video NOR, R/2, the other from
#    above) through an R/2 inverter, where the 2C184 goes more directly: the 2C210 gates the picture with a second signal
#    (probably blanking during sync).

# ---- port decode and the NMI on/off latch (rows 34-37, columns AP-AT) ----
# Bus from the left (rows 30.8-32.5): N.WR, N.IORQ, N.RD, INFE (driven from here, runs left), NMION (driven from here,
# runs left). A0in and A1in come down columns AO and AP from the read-back buffers (rows 25-26).
infe    nor3     INFE           N.RD N.IORQ A0in   @34AP pwr=R  ok210; IN with A0 low: keyboard and tape read, starts vertical sync
outfd   nor3     OUTFD          A1in N.IORQ N.WR   @36AP pwr=R  ok210; OUT with A1 low: NMI off
outfe   nor3     OUTFE          A0in N.IORQ N.WR   @37AP pwr=R  ok210; OUT with A0 low: NMI on
nl1     nor2     NMION          OUTFD NMIOFF  @36AT pwr=R  ok210; cross-coupled
nl2     nor2     NMIOFF         NMION OUTFE   @37AT pwr=R  ok210; runs right to column BC and up to the NMI gate (nm2)

# ---- memory select outputs (rows 30-32, columns BB-BJ): "see cct diagram" (RTL stages and totem-pole outputs) ----
rmi     inv_rtl  RAMCSi         RAMSELn       @30BB  ok210; RTL
rmo     pin_tpn  RAM.N.CS       RAMCSi        @30BF  ok210; PN12; the stage after the input transistor inverts (pin_tpn): confirmed by the cell circuit 'PINS ROMCS, RAMCS' on ULA 2C158/2, where the whole cell, input transistor included, does not invert. That circuit also shows the RAM cell holding the ROM cell off through 6K, which is the RAMCSi input of 'rom'
rom     nor2_rtl ROMCSi         ROMLINE RAMCSi   @32BB  ok210; RTL. ROM N.CS = ROMLINE or RAMACC: the ROM is selected for A14 low, or while Q20 is set, unless the RAM is
romo    pin_tpn  ROM.N.CS       ROMCSi        @32BF  ok210; PN13; the stage after the input transistor inverts (pin_tpn): confirmed by the cell circuit 'PINS ROMCS, RAMCS' on ULA 2C158/2, where the whole cell, input transistor included, does not invert. That circuit also shows the RAM cell holding the ROM cell off through 6K, which is the RAMCSi input of 'rom'
